---
pagination:
  # Convoy has a real page (src/tajima-convoy.njk), so it is excluded in
  # _data/locationStubs.js. Do NOT filter with `pagination.before` here:
  # `before` must be a real function, YAML cannot express one, and a string is
  # ignored silently rather than erroring.
  data: locationStubs
  size: 1
  alias: loc
layout: layouts/base.njk
permalink: "{{ loc.url }}"
pageKey: locationStub
noindex: true
eleventyComputed:
  title: "Tajima Ramen {{ loc.name }} | {{ loc.address.locality }}, {{ loc.address.region }}"
  description: "Tajima Ramen {{ loc.name }}, {{ loc.address.street }}, {{ loc.address.locality }}. Address and phone. Walk in, no reservations."
---
{#
  ============================ STUB PAGES ============================

  THESE ARE NOT FINISHED PAGES AND MUST NOT GO LIVE AS THEY ARE.

  Built tonight for one reason: /locations/ is a P1 page that linked to six
  URLs that did not exist. Six 404s off the site's router is worse than six
  thin pages behind a noindex.

  They carry `noindex` deliberately. These URLs have existing traffic on the
  current site (SITE_ARCHITECTURE.md: existing location URLs do not change
  precisely because they earn it), and shipping thin content on a page that
  already ranks is a regression, not a placeholder. Noindex keeps them out of
  the index until the real page replaces them. Removing the noindex is part of
  finishing the page, not a separate decision.

  CONTENT RULE FOR THIS TEMPLATE: everything on the page comes from
  locations.json, which carries the SITE_ARCHITECTURE.md NAP table. Nothing is
  written here. The one line of prose per location is the `summary` field,
  which was already sourced from CLIENT_FACTS.md for the /locations/ cards, not
  drafted tonight.

  Hours are absent, as everywhere else. Open Decision #9. The page says so
  and offers the phone number instead of guessing.

  What each of these still needs before launch, per the location page template
  in SITE_ARCHITECTURE.md: the "what's different here" section (the one section
  the brief says must not be templated), this location's menu section, its
  happy hour block, its nearest-neighbour link, and its GBP and Yelp URLs for
  `sameAs`. Toast ordering URLs landed 2026-08-05 and photography is partly
  handled, see below.

  PHOTOGRAPHY, added 2026-08-05. The gallery below renders ONLY for locations
  with a curated set in _data/roomPhotos.js, which today is Crown Point alone
  among the stubs. That is not a cautious rollout, it is what exists: Mercury
  has two room frames and both are too small to place, East Village's only
  photograph is a plate of shishito peppers, and Plaza Bonita and Maui have no
  room photography at all. The gate means those four render no gallery section
  rather than an empty frame, which is the difference between a page that does
  not have a section and a page that looks broken.

  These pages stay `noindex` regardless. A gallery is not a finished page.
#}
{%- set gallery = roomPhotos[loc.id] %}

{%- set spriteIcons = ["ramen-bowl"] %}
{% include "components/icon-sprite.njk" %}

{#- PREVIEW BRANCH: the stub hero gains a photo slot when the location has a
    curated hero. Gated, so Maui (which has none) renders the original
    single-column hero rather than an empty frame. -#}
<section class="page-hero{% if gallery.hero %} page-hero--split{% endif %}" aria-labelledby="page-title">
  <div class="page-hero__inner">
   <div>
    <p class="page-hero__crumbs">
      <a href="/">{{ site.name }}</a>
      <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <a href="/locations/">Locations</a>
      <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <span class="page-hero__crumbs-current">{{ loc.name }}</span>
    </p>
    <h1 class="page-hero__title" id="page-title">{{ loc.name }}</h1>
    <p class="page-hero__lede">{{ loc.summary }}</p>

    <address class="plate">
      <span class="plate__item">
        <span class="plate__label">Address</span>
        <span class="plate__value">{{ loc.address.street }}, {{ loc.address.locality }}, {{ loc.address.region }} {{ loc.address.postalCode }}</span>
      </span>
      <span class="plate__item">
        <span class="plate__label">Phone</span>
        <a class="plate__value" href="{{ loc.phone | telHref }}">{{ loc.phone }}</a>
      </span>
      {% include "components/plate-hours.njk" %}
      <span class="plate__item">
        <span class="plate__label">Directions</span>
        <a class="plate__value" href="{{ loc | mapsUrl }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open in Maps<span class="u-visually-hidden">, opens in a new tab</span></a>
      </span>
      <span class="plate__item">
        <span class="plate__label">Seating</span>
        <span class="plate__value">Walk in. No reservations.</span>
      </span>
      {%- if loc.parking %}
      <span class="plate__item">
        <span class="plate__label">Parking</span>
        <span class="plate__value">{{ loc.parking }}</span>
      </span>
      {%- endif %}
      <span class="plate__item">
        <span class="plate__label">Menu</span>
        <a class="plate__value" href="/menu/">See the menu</a>
      </span>
      {#
        HAPPY HOUR ROW, added 2026-09-09, and gated on whether the room has a
        bar at all. SITE_ARCHITECTURE.md requires /happy-hour/ as a universal
        internal link on every location page, and four of these five were
        missing it. Plaza Bonita is the exception and stays without one:
        CLIENT_FACTS.md says quick-serve, no alcohol, so pointing that room at
        a page about drinking would be the link contradicting the room. Maui
        is not in happyHour.json at all, and its brief forbids cross-linking
        it into the San Diego set.

        The row links, it does not state a time. Windows are unconfirmed
        everywhere, which is what /happy-hour/ itself says.
      #}
      {%- set hh = (happyHour.locations | where("id", loc.id)) | first %}
      {%- if hh and hh.servesAlcohol %}
      <span class="plate__item">
        <span class="plate__label">Happy Hour</span>
        <a class="plate__value" href="/happy-hour/">See times</a>
      </span>
      {%- endif %}
      {#
        Added 2026-08-05. These pages had no ordering link of any kind, on a
        site whose third-biggest page is /order-online/. Straight to this
        kitchen's own Toast page, from locations.json, click-tested for all
        seven. The guard stays because it costs nothing, not because a
        location is missing one.
      #}
      {%- if loc.orderUrl %}
      <span class="plate__item">
        <span class="plate__label">Order</span>
        <a class="plate__value" href="{{ loc.orderUrl }}" rel="noopener">Order online</a>
      </span>
      {%- endif %}
    </address>
   </div>

    {%- if gallery.hero %}
    <figure class="page-hero__photo">
      <img class="page-hero__photo-img"
        src="{{ gallery.hero.src }}"
        alt="{{ gallery.hero.alt }}"
        loading="lazy" width="{{ gallery.hero.width }}" height="{{ gallery.hero.height }}">
      <figcaption class="page-hero__photo-cap">{{ gallery.hero.caption }}</figcaption>
    </figure>
    {%- endif %}
  </div>
</section>

{% include "components/location-place.njk" %}

{# ==================== WHAT'S DIFFERENT HERE ====================
   The section SITE_ARCHITECTURE.md calls "the one section that must not be
   templated". Cells come from _data/roomDifferences.json, where each room's
   set is hand written from CLIENT_FACTS.md for that room and nothing is
   generated. The loop renders them; it does not author them.

   Four of the five stubs have a set. Maui has none on purpose: see the _maui
   note in that file. A room with no set simply renders no section, which is
   the same graceful-degradation rule the galleries follow.

   This was the biggest structural gap between the stubs and the two full
   location pages, and it is the main reason Plaza Bonita and Maui read as
   near-duplicates of each other. #}
{%- set diffCells = roomDifferences[loc.id] %}
{%- if diffCells %}
<section class="sect pattern-section" aria-labelledby="diff-title">
  <div class="sect__inner">
    <header class="sect__head">
      <h2 class="sect__title" id="diff-title">What is different about <em>this room.</em></h2>
    </header>

    <div class="diff">
      {%- for cell in diffCells %}
      <article class="cell diff__cell{% if loop.first %} diff__cell--wide{% endif %} reveal">
        <h3 class="diff__title">{{ cell.title }}</h3>
        <p class="diff__body">{{ cell.body }}</p>
      </article>
      {%- endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
{%- endif %}

{#
  The room, where we have it. Same component /tajima-college-heights/ uses, so
  a stub that graduates keeps the section it already had.
#}
{%- if gallery.gallery %}
  {%- set gallerySet = gallery.gallery %}
  {%- set galleryId = "room-title" %}
  {%- set galleryTitle = "The room, <em>photographed.</em>" %}
  {%- set galleryIcon = false %}
  {%- set galleryNote = false %}
  {% include "components/location-gallery.njk" %}
{%- endif %}

{#
  This kitchen's own food, added 2026-08-05. Separate set from the room
  photography and separately gated, because Mercury and East Village have food
  frames but no usable room frames, and the reverse is true at Crown Point.
  Renders nothing for a location with neither.
#}
{%- if gallery.dishes %}
  {%- set gallerySet = gallery.dishes %}
  {%- set galleryId = "dishes-title" %}
  {#- Retitled 2026-09-09. This said "What comes out of this room", which is
      now the heading of the menu section below it, and the bowl icon moved
      there with it: one mark per page, on the section that carries the list
      rather than the photographs of it. -#}
  {%- set galleryTitle = "From this kitchen, <em>photographed.</em>" %}
  {%- set galleryIcon = false %}
  {%- set galleryNote = 'Shot at this location, not borrowed from another room.' %}
  {% include "components/location-gallery.njk" %}
{%- endif %}

{# ==================== WHAT THIS ROOM SERVES ====================
   Section 4 of the location page template, which these five pages did not
   have at all. Rows come from menu.json filtered by this room's `locations`,
   derived from the live Toast catalogs, so Plaza Bonita shows the seven
   dishes it actually carries and not the eleven the standalone rooms do.
   See components/location-menu.njk for why there are no prices here. #}
{%- set menuLoc = loc.id %}
{%- set menuTitle = "What comes out of <em>" + loc.name + ".</em>" %}
{%- set menuNote = 'From this room\'s own list. <a class="sect__link" href="/menu/">See the whole menu</a>, with prices.' %}
{%- set menuTitleId = "menu-title" %}
{% include "components/location-menu.njk" %}

{#
  ==================== HAPPY HOUR, EAST VILLAGE ONLY ====================
  Added 2026-08-05, and deliberately scoped to one room.

  East Village is the only location with a happy hour fact confirmed in
  CLIENT_FACTS.md: "Padres game-night beer specials and extended hours on home
  game nights." That is this room and no other, and it must not be widened.

  The other five rooms are NOT given this block on purpose: there is nothing
  confirmed to put in one, and a section that only says "being confirmed"
  earns nothing. When real windows arrive for a room, it gets this block.

  CORRECTED 2026-09-09. This used to justify the omission by saying the other
  rooms "already carry a Happy Hour / See times row in the address plate".
  They do not. Only the two full location templates carry that row; the stub
  plate never has. The reasoning above stands without it.

  No price. SITE_ARCHITECTURE.md's East Village brief carries "$3.50" but
  happyHour.json pulled that figure as unverified, so the two sources disagree
  and the number stays off.

  No times. Extended hours on game nights is confirmed; how extended is not.
#}
{%- if loc.id == "east-village" %}
<section class="sect sect--rule" aria-labelledby="hh-title">
  <div class="sect__inner">
    <header class="sect__head">
      <h2 class="sect__title" id="hh-title">Game nights at <em>Petco.</em></h2>
      <p class="sect__note">
        This room runs beer specials on Padres home game nights, and stays open later than usual when the game is at home. The window on other days is being confirmed, so call the room and they will tell you what is running. Full picture on <a class="sect__link" href="/happy-hour/">the happy hour page</a>.
      </p>
    </header>
  </div>
</section>
{%- endif %}

{# What is still missing differs per room now that four of the five carry a
   "what is different" section, so the copy has to differ too. Saying "what is
   different about it is being written" on a page that just said it would be
   the page contradicting itself two screens apart. #}
<section class="sect" aria-labelledby="soon-title">
  <div class="sect__inner">
    <header class="sect__head">
      <h2 class="sect__title" id="soon-title">Still to <em>come.</em></h2>
      <p class="sect__note">
        Address, phone and hours are right, and they are the same everywhere we publish them.
        {%- if diffCells %}
        What this room still needs is its own photographs.
        {%- else %}
        The rest of this room, its photographs and what is different about it, is being written.
        {%- endif %}
        In the meantime, <a class="sect__link" href="/menu/">the menu</a> and <a class="sect__link" href="/locations/">the other rooms</a>.
      </p>
    </header>
  </div>
</section>

{% include "components/location-faq.njk" %}

{# The noodle line, universal section 6 of the location page template. #}
<section class="noodle-band" aria-labelledby="band-title">
  <div class="noodle-band__inner">
    <div>
      <h2 class="noodle-band__slogan" id="band-title">Better noodles weren't for sale. <em>So we made them.</em></h2>
      <p class="noodle-band__body">
        {#
          Scoped to San Diego on purpose. Crown Point supplies San Diego and
          Maui is 2,500 miles away, so no "our noodles" claim extends there.
          SITE_ARCHITECTURE.md Open Decision #1.
        #}
        {%- if loc.region == "san-diego" %}
        The noodles are made in our own Noodle Room in Crown Point, and the broth is simmered there every morning and driven out before service.
        {%- else %}
        Sam spent two years building a noodle room in Crown Point, on a machine brought over from Japan.
        {%- endif %}
      </p>
    </div>
    <a class="noodle-band__cta" href="/noodle-room/">
      See the Noodle Room
      <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
        <path d="M1 7H13M13 7L7.5 1.5M13 7L7.5 12.5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round"/>
      </svg>
    </a>
  </div>
</section>
